{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"POINTER FOR A LATER READER — the click override this ticket's commit carried has its full analysis on\nanother ticket. Adding this only so the trail is followable; nothing here needs action, and the code on\nmain is correct and complete.\n\nCommit 31844d5f9fb (\"fix PYSEC-2026-2132 via click override\") landed under this ticket, whose stated\npurpose is the dependabot PRs. The inline comment it added to pyproject.toml is good and does carry the\nREMOVE-WHEN condition (\"Drop this override once inspect-ai lifts its cap upstream\") plus the staleness\nreason (inspect-ai caps click < 8.2.2 solely for pallets/click#3084, fixed upstream in click 8.3.2).\n\nWHAT IS NOT ON MAIN, AND IS THE EXPENSIVE PART TO REDISCOVER, is on ticket e47e-a33d-b9cf-4421 (now\nclosed as a duplicate of this ticket, with six evidence comments retained):\n\n * **override-dependencies vs constraint-dependencies.** An attempt to verify the upgrade with\n   `constraint-dependencies = [\"click>=8.3.3\"]` returns UNSATISFIABLE — and that result is MEANINGLESS,\n   because constraint-dependencies can only NARROW an existing constraint set; it cannot lift a cap a\n   dependency declares. `override-dependencies` REPLACES the requirement, which is why it works. A\n   reader who repeats the constraint experiment will wrongly conclude the upgrade is impossible and may\n   reach for a pip-audit `--ignore-vuln` suppression instead. That nearly happened here.\n * `uv lock --upgrade-package click` is a NO-OP for the same reason — it only permits movement inside\n   the existing constraint set, so 8.2.1 really is the newest click satisfying inspect-ai. The resolver\n   was never wrong and the uv version is irrelevant.\n * VERIFICATION THAT SHOULD BE REPEATED WHEN THE OVERRIDE IS REMOVED: `uv lock --check` under BOTH uv\n   0.7.18 and 0.12.1 (the lock must stay at revision 2 — relocking with 0.12.1 rewrites it to revision 3\n   with sweeping marker churn), `uv sync --locked --extra dev`, and `pip-audit --desc` over the whole\n   resulting environment to confirm the old pin was masking nothing else.\n * SCOPE FACT worth knowing: override-dependencies is a workspace resolution directive and is NOT\n   published in wheel metadata, so consumers installing nava-rebar[eval] from PyPI still get inspect-ai's\n   own cap. The override moves only this repo's lock.\n\nAlso linked from e47e: 9fb3-ab66-2a81-4940 (the [eval]/inspect-ai path has no CI coverage and, because\n`[tool.uv] conflicts` declares eval and dev mutually conflicting, structurally cannot get any from the\nnormal suite)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785715483151482001,"uuid":"bc46ffdf-9262-4bd4-a4d2-5209218733c9"}